// "Built-in Metadata Parsing" closes the metadata NAME and deliberately not its
// field set: an unknown built-in FORM name is a parse error, while an unknown or
// unhandled FIELD of a known form "is still accepted, collected, and preserved as
// parsed; lack of frontend field knowledge alone is not an error".
//
// `extensions` is not a field the frontend understands, so this file must parse
// with the field preserved rather than be rejected. The two fields the frontend
// does understand keep their own value-shape validation.
@co.ddap.use(from="stringextension", extensions=[upperCase])
